SlothClash core patch 0046: client-fingerprint firefox156 / firefox160.

Firefox 156 and 160 send the same fresh ClientHello: Firefox 148 without
the ECDSA CBC suites and the FFDHE groups, with a GREASE ECH payload of 240
bytes. metacubex/utls v1.9.0-alpha.1 stops at 148, so the spec is data in
component/tls/firefox160.go, applied through HelloCustom like chrome155
(0029); customHello in chrome155.go now serves both behind the same
fingerprintSpec / uClient hooks (session cache handled, fallback to Firefox
148 when the spec cannot apply). The GREASE ECH enc is drawn uniformly per
connection, as NSS does. Names firefox156, firefox160 and Xray's
hellofirefox_156, hellofirefox_160; "firefox" stays Firefox 148.

Ported from Prizrak-Core v1.19.34-r4.
The fixtures are its captures of the browsers. Delete when mihomo moves to
a utls release with these profiles.

Tests: component/tls (byte for byte against the captures except key shares
and GREASE ECH contents, enc uniformity, firefox stays 148, a TLS 1.3
handshake with a session cache, REALITY key-share gate under On and Off),
config (the names load in a profile).

